# AI Agent Course Notebooks

This directory contains Jupyter notebooks designed for hands-on exercises and practical applications of the concepts covered in the AI Agent Developer and Operator course. Each notebook is structured to facilitate learning and experimentation with AI agents, providing a comprehensive guide for participants.

## Notebook Structure

### 01_agent_fundamentals.ipynb
- Overview of AI agents
- Definitions and types of agents
- Foundational theories and concepts

### 02_development_practices.ipynb
- Best practices for coding AI agents
- Version control with Git
- Testing methodologies for AI applications

### 03_operator_workflows.ipynb
- Monitoring and maintaining AI agents
- Optimization techniques for performance
- Workflow diagrams and case studies

### 04_intelligent_documentation.ipynb
- Creating intelligent documentation
- Tools for automated documentation
- Techniques for evolving documentation with projects

### 05_visualization_tools.ipynb
- Introduction to visualization tools
- Techniques for interpreting AI data
- Practical examples of model performance visualization

### 06_latest_methodologies.ipynb
- Overview of cutting-edge methodologies in AI
- Case studies on recent advancements
- Discussion on the impact of new practices

### 07_future_guides.ipynb
- Emerging trends in AI agent development
- Predictions for future technologies
- Preparing for the next generation of AI applications

## Usage Instructions

1. Open the desired notebook using Jupyter Notebook or JupyterLab.
2. Follow the instructions and complete the exercises provided in each section.
3. Experiment with the code examples to deepen your understanding of AI agent development and operation.

